{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1456758-hidden-wars-hunter-vs-the-web-of-pain","id":1456758,"title":"Hidden Wars? Hunter vs the Web of Pain","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-13T07:23:12-07:00","id":1456758,"title":"Hidden Wars? Hunter vs the Web of Pain","content":"Something I don't really seen talked, as seems much more interesting than hunters vs deviants, about is the potential of hunters vs the conspiracies that make deviants. Obviously, you have some groups like Cheiron that probably regularly make Deviants by accident and intention. But rather than just playing a run-away, there's some real potential for someone interesting play of secret wars.<br /> <br /> 1. They're everything the Union hates. Big wigs calling themselves human who see the little guy as nothing but a disposable resource. The local division of the Union is nothing but upset to find out about a local entrenched conspiracy. Can the little guy uproot it?<br /> <br /> 2. Good help is so hard to find. True, the loss of your maid to that conspiracy is annoying, and your house is going to be a bit messy while you find another one, and they probably won't be as good. Still, you'll have your huff and be on with you life. Still, you wonder. The usual hunt, while entertaining, could use a little shaking up. Not to mention that you and your friends are at least as entrenched as that conspiracy. And wars have been fought over less, you know. And why, a deadly game of social and legal politics among the rich sounds like something out of a Spy Thriller B-Movie - how dreadfully entertaining it sounds! And all while doing a charitable deed, as icing on the cake, having the reassurance that you are in the right. It sounds like Ashwood Abbey is about to have a few interesting evenings.<br /> <br /> 3. It was the death of Jesus Christ that gave man the ability to find redemption through the one true church of God. That has been core doctrine for millennia, and is unlikely to change any time soon. Nothing can change that sacrifice. Or can it? What if a man's soul were to break? On death, presuming they were faithful Catholics, would they go to Heaven? Or would they just cease to exist? The idea of a soul breaking, denied a heavenly reward in spite of the covenant with Christ, chills the Malleus Maleficarum to the bone. True, the embrace can damn you, but even then, proper penance can redeem you in death. The destruction of the soul is different. The Malleus Maleficarum has deemed the willful destruction of the soul on such a mass level to be the height of blasphemy, eclipsed only be the betrayal of Judas itself.<br /> What's new is that knowledge. And ever since it has been learned, the Pope secretly excommunicated all conspiracy members knowingly involved - and the truth now is that the Malleus Maleficarum has declared war on those blasphemous conspiracies for the sake of faithful Catholics the world round.<br /> <br /> 4. It confirmed their worst suspicions and fears, and how they not similarly broken still baffles many members. Maybe it was some strange connection to their worst enemy, but it's clear that the children of the Merrick Institute aren't the only victims. They thankfully are more organized, but this does raise fear and opportunity. Other hunters may see deviants as monsters, but to the Merrick Institute, they are brothers and sisters in arms, separated only by the particular group of bastards that hurt them. It is time for the Institute to unite those victim into a united front to wipe out the web of pain once and for all.<br /> <br /> 5. Agent, your background says you served a tour in Afghanistan, right? You've got a bunch of bastards out there dedicated to overthrowing the new republic government and spreading tyranny and fear throughout the world. It's a good thing it couldn't happen here, right?<br /> I'd say &quot;That's where you're wrong&quot;, but the look on your face says you know where I'm going with this. I'm not talking the militia movement, some communist sleeper cell, or even damn vampires. No, there are alleged humans that'll kidnap our citizens, brainwash them, and try to turn them into monsters, all while they try to puppeteer the government and corporations. Now, it's just my opinion, but I think they're the worst of all. You don't see werewolves wiping out swathes of cities. But my grandfather learned at Auschwitz that it's evil humans in large number that are the worst monsters. And Task Force Valkyrie is here to keep monsters at bay.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25382-tzauri","name":"Tzauri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-13T13:59:23-07:00","id":1456783,"title":"","content":"Actually, I wrote this <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1346844-lighting-candles-in-a-web-of-pain-hunters-and-deviants-oh-my\">thing </a>when I thought about how do the core groups interact with the Web of Pain","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}